Ambassador Jennifer Locetta
Alternative Representative for Special Political Affairs
New York, New York
AS DELIVERED
Thank you, President.
The goal of a peaceful and prosperous future throughout Israel, the West Bank, and Gaza is achievable. The United States and our partners on the Board of Peace continue to work toward that goal.
To achieve that future, the immediate and complete disarmament and demobilization of Hamas is critical. As a terrorist organization, Hamas must have no future in Gaza’s governance. Hamas must fulfill that commitment, as agreed in line with President Trump’s 20-point Comprehensive Plan to End the Gaza Conflict, which this Council endorsed in Resolution 2803.
We call again on all UN Member States to support the work of the Board of Peace including the Office of the High Representative, the National Committee for the Administration of Gaza, and the International Stabilization Force. We welcome the ongoing cooperation between Israel, the EU, and regional partners under the EU’s “Pact for the Mediterranean” initiative.
In his address to the UNGA last week, Palestinian Authority (PA) President Abbas continued to push for unilateral recognition of a Palestinian state. He incorrectly claimed that the PA ended its support for terrorism, once again revealing that the PA does not intend to fulfill this commitment.
That is why the United States continues to maintain sanctions on the PA and the Palestine Liberation Organization. The PA must end its financial and ideological support for terrorism, follow through on its commitments, and enact its long-promised reforms.
As President Trump stated, the United States opposes Israeli annexation of the West Bank. Stability in the West Bank is vital for Israel’s security and aligns with our goal of achieving peace in the region. We must collectively work to ensure the well-being of Israelis, Palestinians, and all those living throughout the region.
We share, however, the concerns of other Security Council members regarding economic instability in the West Bank and the need for economic opportunities for Palestinian residents. Yet, some UN Member States have chosen to enact or propose measures that target businesses in parts of Jerusalem, the Golan Heights, and the West Bank. As Secretary Rubio said, we do not want to see any destabilizing activity in the West Bank at this moment, as it could have implications on our ability to make progress with regard to President Trump’s Gaza peace plan.
Thank you.
