AS DELIVERED
Thank you, Mr. President.
We strongly reject the assertions made by some members of this Council and we fully support moving forward with this meeting.
Several members of this body want to prevent this discussion to protect Iran: a country that continues to openly defy many of its most basic UN obligations.
This Committee was tasked by this body to constrain and monitor a nuclear program that Iran sought to operate out of the view of the international community.
We will discuss the essential extension of this Panel’s mandate today.
Just one year ago, this Council voted decisively to permit the snapback of sanctions and the re-establishment of the 1737 Committee.
This Committee is legitimate. It has a sanctions list, a proposed slate of members for the Panel, and it has decided a number of sanctions exemptions.
I urge everyone to join us to adopt the agenda and allow the Council to proceed with the vote.
Thank you.
